Subject: Install pycurl Python module to dist-packages without the setuptools deb install scheme
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Keep Debian's dist-packages and shared-data destinations for python3-pycurl when the builder setuptools lacks the deb install layout.
Base-Tree: debian pycurl 7.45.6-1
Verify: cmd `sh -c 'dpkg-deb -c python3-pycurl_7.45.6-1+deb13u0+dhi0_amd64.deb | grep -q " ./usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/curl/__init__.py" && ! dpkg-deb -c python3-pycurl_7.45.6-1+deb13u0+dhi0_amd64.deb | grep -q " ./usr/local/" && echo clean'` expect "clean"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI build environment workaround only)
Drop-When: never: DHI builder setuptools has no deb install scheme and Debian setuptools is not pinned in this builder

Debian's debian/rules passes --install-layout=deb to setup.py install. That option needs the deb scheme from Debian's patched python3-setuptools, but the DHI hermetic builder ships setuptools 84.x without it, so the install step fails with KeyError 'deb_system'. This patch passes the destinations explicitly: modules remain under /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages and shared data remains under /usr instead of falling back to /usr/local.

--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -42,7 +42,9 @@
 
 override_dh_auto_install:
 	for py in $(PY3VERS); do \
-		python$$py setup.py install --root=$(CURDIR)/debian/python3-pycurl --install-layout=deb; \
+		python$$py setup.py install --root=$(CURDIR)/debian/python3-pycurl --prefix=/usr \
+			--install-purelib=/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages --install-platlib=/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages \
+			--install-data=/usr; \
 	done
 
 	# Remove documentation as installed by setup.py
